  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 30. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. ガードレール — 道路の端などに設ける車の転落などを防ぐ柵。\n2. 生糸 — 蚕の繭から取ったままの絹の糸。\n3. 機械化 — 人がしていた作業などを機械で行うようにすること。\n4. 聞き手 — 話を聞く側の人。\n5. 聞き取り — 話や音を聞いて内容を捉えること。\n6. 効き目 — 薬や方法などによって現れる効果。\n7. 企業 — 品物やサービスなどを生み出す事業を行う組織。\n8. 気配り — 周りの様子を考えて細かいことにも気をつけること。\n9. 喜劇 — 見ている人を笑わせる内容の劇。\n10. 帰国 — 外国から自分の国に帰ること。\n11. 器材 — 作業などに使う器具や材料。\n12. 岸辺 — 川や海や湖の岸の近く。\n13. 旗手 — 集団の先頭などで旗を持つ人。\n14. 気象学 — 大気の状態や天気の仕組みを調べる学問。\n15. 気象台 — 気象の観測や予報などを行う施設。\n16. 期日 — あらかじめ決められた日。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
